1
00:00:08,826 --> 00:00:09,526
Meet Eddy.

2
00:00:09,457 --> 00:00:12,616
Event-time features, with sub-millisecond serving.

3
00:00:12,636 --> 00:00:14,163
Raw user events go in.

4
00:00:14,183 --> 00:00:16,521
Fresh, per-user machine-learning features come

5
00:00:16,541 --> 00:00:18,988
out, ready the moment a model asks.

6
00:00:20,029 --> 00:00:21,200
This is the live console.

7
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,128
Sixty thousand events a minute stream through

8
00:00:24,148 --> 00:00:26,866
Kafka, thousands of users have features that

9
00:00:26,886 --> 00:00:29,628
are seconds old, and every stage of the pipeline

10
00:00:29,648 --> 00:00:30,965
reports its own health.

11
00:00:32,007 --> 00:00:34,487
Spark Structured Streaming runs three queries

12
00:00:34,507 --> 00:00:36,559
at once: a five-minute window,

13
00:00:36,579 --> 00:00:39,178
a one-hour window, and a live profile.

14
00:00:39,198 --> 00:00:42,118
Each one shows exactly how much of its capacity

15
00:00:42,138 --> 00:00:42,979
it is using.

16
00:00:43,996 --> 00:00:45,857
Now, the part a model cares about.

17
00:00:45,877 --> 00:00:48,822
Pick a user, and Eddy returns their spend,

18
00:00:48,842 --> 00:00:51,333
conversion and browsing behaviour for the last

19
00:00:51,353 --> 00:00:53,095
five minutes and the last hour,

20
00:00:53,115 --> 00:00:54,503
straight from Redis.

21
00:00:55,531 --> 00:00:57,535
And bad data never breaks the stream.

22
00:00:57,555 --> 00:01:00,571
Every event is checked against a versioned Avro

23
00:01:00,591 --> 00:01:01,291
schema.

24
00:01:01,115 --> 00:01:03,856
Anything that breaks the contract lands in a

25
00:01:03,876 --> 00:01:06,312
dead-letter queue, with the reason attached.

26
00:01:07,339 --> 00:01:08,772
Under the hood: a producer,

27
00:01:08,792 --> 00:01:12,391
Kafka, Spark, Redis and FastAPI.

28
00:01:12,411 --> 00:01:15,736
Built for correctness, with event-time watermarks,

29
00:01:15,756 --> 00:01:17,426
exactly-once checkpoints,

30
00:01:17,446 --> 00:01:20,513
and writes that never roll a feature backwards.

31
00:01:21,523 --> 00:01:22,223
Eddy.

32
00:01:21,773 --> 00:01:24,753
Event-time features with sub-millisecond serving,

33
00:01:24,773 --> 00:01:26,122
in one Docker command.

34
00:01:26,142 --> 00:01:27,959
Open source, on GitHub.

